From: OHOS Wine build fix
Subject: [PATCH] dxil-spirv: explicitly include <exception> for std::terminate

scratch_pool.hpp uses std::terminate() but relied on transitive includes
for <exception>. With llvm-mingw clang 23 / libc++ headers the transitive
include is gone and the arm64ec cross build fails with:

  scratch_pool.hpp:52:9: error: no member named 'terminate' in namespace 'std'

Add the missing direct include.
---
 subprojects/dxil-spirv/scratch_pool.hpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/subprojects/dxil-spirv/scratch_pool.hpp b/subprojects/dxil-spirv/scratch_pool.hpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/subprojects/dxil-spirv/scratch_pool.hpp
+++ b/subprojects/dxil-spirv/scratch_pool.hpp
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@

 #pragma once

+#include <exception>
 #include "thread_local_allocator.hpp"

 namespace dxil_spv
--
2.34.1
